            <div xml:id="d215">

                <pb facs="0364" n="270" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg270"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 L 36/155: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Greece</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Atherton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-03-20T14:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 20,
                                1924—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received March
                    20—noon.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>53. Your 32, March 10, 4 p.m. This morning Minister of Foreign Affairs, who also
                    is Prime Minister, informed me that he was pleased to agree to the appointment
                    of Laughlin as Minister and that he will send me a note tomorrow in
                    confirmation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Atherton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
